// M5-A3P-1003. Ch18 §4 Haluna: "Backs to the Water" (optional, flagged; ~150 words). act3_ch18.md §4,
// rule 4; toma_okeru.md; ending_cost_audit §7. Toma gathers the village and they lift their own dead the Kirru way,
// with their backs to the water. NOTHING IS LIFTED BY ASHA: she stands at the back; the Cantor doesn't perform it, the
// town does. RULE 5 / README rule 1: a Kirru-way lifting lifts a FEW motes; most stay held (the storm still holds the
// rest). This is the one Ch17-18 scene allowed a glimmer_lift (check_drafts.py LIFT_ALLOWED).
// Requires ch15_toma_confessed (the flow gates it). Pays the Ending's beach rite and Ch20 Ilun.
title: ch18_backs_to_the_water
location: ch02/haluna
---
@letterbox on
@camera K15
@music haluna_lifting fade=3.0
@mark toma shore_line walk
@mark asha village_back walk
@wait 3.0
Toma [neutral]: Everyone who has someone in the water. Come and stand with me. #line:ch18_haluna_001
@mark crowd shore_line_crowd walk
@wait 4.0
Neme [worried]: Without a Cantor? #line:ch18_haluna_002
Toma [determined]: We don't need a Cantor for this. We need each other. #line:ch18_haluna_003
@wait 2.0
Toma [neutral]: Backs to the water. Say their names to the person beside you. Not to the sea. #line:ch18_haluna_004
@anim crowd turn_back sea
@anim toma turn_back sea
@wait 3.0
@sfx names_murmured vol=0.5
@wait 5.0
@camera K16
@vfx glimmer_lift at=wake_wall count=5 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@vfx glimmer_held at=wake_wall count=40 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 6.0
Neme [grief]: Only a few. #line:ch18_haluna_005
@wait 2.0
Toma [tender]: Then those few are home. We'll do it again. #line:ch18_haluna_006
@camera K17
@anim asha look_at sea
@wait 4.0
<<set $ch18_haluna_lifted = true>>
@letterbox off
===
